# Plan — Task 162-003 — agent-pool + skill-pool + skill-registry READ-ONLY audit

## Goal
Produce single audit report at `docs/audits/sprint-162-live/T-162-LIVE-003-core-agent-skill-pool.md`
applying 10 audit dimensions to:
- src/core/agent-pool.ts (491 LoC)
- src/core/skill-pool.ts (306 LoC)
- src/core/skill-registry.ts (134 LoC)
+ peripheral context: agent-types.ts, agent-cache.ts, agent-selector.ts, src/core/builtins/{agents,skills}/

## Lead Questions (per DIRECTIVES Task 3)
1. **15 built-in agents claim** — Verify count vs `.deckent/agents/` and `src/core/builtins/agents/`
2. **21 built-in skills claim** — Verify count vs `.deckent/skills/` and `src/core/builtins/skills/`
3. **LRU eviction** — Where is it implemented? Correct policy? `MAX_TEMP_AGENTS=50`, `MAX_SPRINT_AGE=5`?
4. **AST sandbox** — skill-registry.ts validation logic; bypass surfaces

## 10 Audit Dimensions
1. Dead code — unused exports, unreferenced helpers
2. ADR violations — ADR-001/002 (ESM + .js extensions), ADR-008 (no brain import), ADR-041 (taxonomy)
3. Conflicting areas — duplicated logic between agent-pool / skill-pool / skill-registry
4. Drift — comments/JSDoc vs actual behavior; claim verification (15 agents, 21 skills, LRU)
5. Type safety — `any`, `as unknown as`, `@ts-ignore`, missing return types
6. Dependency hygiene — `.js` extensions in imports, circular dep risk
7. Documentation pollution — stale comments
8. Memory V2 coherence — N/A (no MemoryStore touch in these files, but flag if any)
9. Config integrity — N/A unless config touch
10. Migration triage — KEEP-PRIVATE | MIGRATE-PUBLIC | DELETE-CANDIDATE | UNCERTAIN per file

## Steps
1. Read all 6 source files top-to-bottom
2. Sample bundled built-in manifests (1-2 agent.json, 1-2 manifest.json) for schema check
3. Cross-reference vs `.deckent/agents/*/agent.json` runtime state
4. Build Findings table with severity (P0/P1/P2/P3) + file:line citation
5. Migration triage per file
6. Write report; do NOT touch source code

## Boundaries
